{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557511-kuei-jin-dharma-falling-and-disciplines","id":1557511,"title":"[Kuei-Jin] Dharma falling and disciplines","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-12T09:13:31-08:00","id":1557511,"title":"[Kuei-Jin] Dharma falling and disciplines","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> A Kuei-Jin Dharma rating sets how many dots they can have of attributes, abilities, and disciplines, either 5 or their Dharma rating, the highest of those.<br /> <br /> <br /> BUT, Dharma can fall.<br /> <br /> <br /> What happens when you fall to a Dharma lower than required for the stats? Do you lose them and the experience? Get a reimbursement? Have them but not use them? Use normally?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T17:37:23-08:00","id":1557625,"title":"","content":"I'd say they loose them, just like what happened to Tariq when he was subjected to Quenching the Lambent Flame ritual (from 5th gen they dropped him to 13th), they have the experience of knowing that that can happen, let that be a lesson.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T22:39:49-08:00","id":1557640,"title":"","content":"I'd say they keep the dots but can't use them until their dharma is high enough again.<br /> <br /> Considering how much 6+ dots cost, it seems unnecessarily punitive to lose them altogether. And it doesn't make much sense to lose them but be able to reinvest the experience cost. It would heavily push the meta to regard 1-5 dots as more valuable and cost effective than 6+ dots, which is already a thing to some extent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-15T07:57:48-08:00","id":1557648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557511-kuei-jin-dharma-falling-and-disciplines#post1557511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> A Kuei-Jin Dharma rating sets how many dots they can have of attributes, abilities, and disciplines, either 5 or their Dharma rating, the highest of those.<br /> <br /> <br /> BUT, Dharma can fall.<br /> <br /> <br /> What happens when you fall to a Dharma lower than required for the stats? Do you lose them and the experience? Get a reimbursement? Have them but not use them? Use normally?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say they keep everything. They can continue to use any Attribute or Abilities that are higher than their new max. Those aren't exactly magical, though they can't spend Chi to temporarily increase stats beyond the new maximum. They don't lose any powers, but they can't use them anymore. In theory if they regain their Dharmic standing, they can begin accessing everything again. <br /> <br /> The biggest issue for any elder vampire losing their dharmic rating is the social reaction. It's expected that younger vampires, running monkeys, will have moments of blindness and fall off the path a few times. It's very different when it's a venerated elder. If it gets out that an elder fell like that, there would be some major consequences. None of the younger vampires will respect someone who can't stay on the road, and likewise members of their own dharma will look down on them as well. The biggest thing would be that you would quickly begin hearing rumors spreading the individual is an akuma. Whether true or not, falling prey to the Yama King's wiles would be a good reason for someone to fall on their dharmic path, and lots of people would be chomping to get rid of that elder and take their place. <br /> <br /> If something like that got out, probably the most drastic but simplest thing would be to simply declare that you are in the process of leaving your dharma and begin pursuing a new one. It's pretty common for younger vampires to do this, but it's not unprecedented for an elder to do it either. The elder would lose a lot of social standing, but probably still be able to retain some measure of respect.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, of course, the Yama Kings would be more than happy to make a deal to ensure that the elder's failings don't get out. They could probably even offer certain boons to let the Elder continue to access their lost disciplines. It would only be temporary, until the elder was able to reclaim their old dharmic position... well, most elders would be too canny to fall for that, but for some the risk of losing everything would outweigh the risk of bartering with the Yama Kings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T17:42:52-08:00","id":1557747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557511-kuei-jin-dharma-falling-and-disciplines?p=1557640#post1557640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say they keep the dots but can't use them until their dharma is high enough again.<br /> <br /> Considering how much 6+ dots cost, it seems unnecessarily punitive to lose them altogether. And it doesn't make much sense to lose them but be able to reinvest the experience cost. <b>It would heavily push the meta to regard 1-5 dots as more valuable and cost effective than 6+ dots, which is already a thing to some extent.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the reply, care to explain the bolded part?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-19T10:17:55-08:00","id":1557760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557511-kuei-jin-dharma-falling-and-disciplines?p=1557747#post1557747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks for the reply, care to explain the bolded part?</div> </div> </div> </div>If 6+ dots can be lost, while 1-5 dots are permanent, it makes more sense to invest in the latter and become a Jack of All Trades than to spend a ton of XP on a 6th or 7th dot in a favourite trait.<br /> <br /> A 6th dot in an Attribute costs 20xp, in an Ability 10. For 10xp I can get two Abilities from 0 to 2, significantly expanding what my character can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-20T06:45:19-08:00","id":1557777,"title":"","content":"As for powers, I don't remember how it works for Kuei-jin, but most 6+ dots discipline powers are not worth the cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-20T06:51:09-08:00","id":1557778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557511-kuei-jin-dharma-falling-and-disciplines?p=1557777#post1557777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for powers, I don't remember how it works for Kuei-jin, but most 6+ dots discipline powers are not worth the cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, for Kindred and Kuei-jin both, most seem underwhelming; but mine was mostly a theoretical questions about the Dharma falling and rising than the attributes itself.<br /> <br /> I do agree that a character would benefit more from being well rounded than narrowing their focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}